ub.com/users/pachecot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachecot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pachecot/ebo-script/commits/6b6a786082c50d79aebcc6e8e369a94648560d15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-04T00:56:02Z","email":"tomp@netp.org","name":"Tom Pacheco"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-04T00:56:02Z","email":"tomp@netp.org","name":"Tom Pacheco"},"message":"(fix) emit VariableUsedAsLineName instead of misleading DuplicateLine/UndefinedLine\n\nWhen a declared variable (or function) name is used as a line label or as\na Goto target the errors were wrong:\n  - Numeric myVar / myVar:  → was DuplicateLine \"Line ''myVar'' already exists.\"\n  - Numeric myVar / Goto myVar → was UndefinedLine \"Line ''myVar'' not defined.\"\n\nBoth are confusing because myVar is a known symbol — just the wrong kind.\n\n- Add EboErrors.VariableUsedAsLineName\n- SymbolTable.declare_line: distinguish variable clash, function clash, and\n  true duplicate line; emit VariableUsedAsLineName with a clear message for\n  the first two cases\n- check_lines_valid_and_used: when a Goto target is a declared variable emit\n  VariableUsedAsLineName instead of UndefinedLine\n- Add 6 unit tests covering all four scenarios plus a sanity check that\n  genuine DuplicateLine errors are still produced\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0a3f316f890291475dc5f5191d025c3f51d50fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pachecot/ebo-script/git/trees/a0a3f316f890291475dc5f5191d025c3f51d50fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pachecot/ebo-script/git/commits/6b6a786082c50d79aebcc6e8e369a94648560d15","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5196169?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pachecot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api