ved_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blarghmatey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-authoring/commits/994fa2824b192d8a1736934028b7d406c21eda7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:41:13Z","email":"tmacey@boundlessnotions.com","name":"Tobias Macey"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:41:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: query separate course and library search indexes (#3248)\n\n* feat: query separate course and library search indexes\n\nStudio''s single studio_content index is being split into a course index\nand a library index so library authoring isn''t slowed down by indexing\ncost that grows with course content (openedx/openedx-platform#38993).\n\nThe search config endpoint now returns course_index_name and\nlibrary_index_name. Each search surface picks the index for the content\nit shows. When the backend only returns index_name, both fall back to it,\nso this works against unsplit backends unchanged.\n\nNo surface searches courses and libraries together: the Studio search\nmodal has filtered to type = \"course_block\" since #1148, so no\nmulti-index query is needed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"88c973e50f6834e031c490afba6aa84c3109aa71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-authoring/git/trees/88c973e50f6834e031c490afba6aa84c3109aa71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-authoring/git/commits/994fa2824b192d8a1736934028b7d406c21eda7e","verification":{"payload":"tree 88c973e50f6834e031c490afba6aa84c3109aa71\nparent 2c19d9a04789a123a027fc46a4de3c307e1933a5\nauthor Tobias Macey <tmacey@boundlessnotions.com> 1790102473 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790102473 -0700\n\nfeat: query separate course and library search indexes (#3248)\n\n* feat: query separate course and library search indexes\n\nStudio''s single studio_content index is being split into a course index\nand a library index so library authoring isn''t slowed down by indexing\ncost that grows with course content (openedx/openedx-platform#38993).\n\nThe search config endpoint now returns course_index_name and\nlibrary_index_name. Each search surface picks the index for the content\nit shows. When the backend only returns index_name, both fall back to it,\nso this works against unsplit backends unchanged.\n\nNo surface searches courses and libraries together: the Studio search\nmodal has filtered to type = \"course_block\" since #1148, so no\nmulti-index query is needed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqssvJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0ZUQADhLnBzJpnUM+t+4Nyc9KGRL\noKkanEiiOnCHyF+21Xx5RpgJE66nxCFwT7ZePVQiKQsqFrg73T6DWMR6s55XFJzD\n7IdU1xJhOSx5oXIBMVz2lM0sFqkkxCyUeB9V4J0tH14RdhHbVmTG80dMjSC4+rmS\n6x6PcvTvVP3Vp8aKm5glX3yGOV8vm6eZS7JleBIsK4vAtqr5f11TwBswVMBhdsBC\nQcQ5HSvY2CWV5M/aPUENMm8sZ8J9wreaFcDqn5aOybu7wReURDmzK1tYLIkUikYT\nAegaZS4rM9gPkHB0BXj0Xuhsd6P3Gw1jeXKeUKrCQdTQyZ0Q5hzGiAmxqyZt+Kuy\nrtQ/PiJcy1buVmcsOqDivnh/RdHbVNoYd00aWQDTz84+tNUOejnQZMef8YazmVHv\n+IfAVZeoAteUSjDdMVVcBzcXaJuMKlgMbXxScAqttVBYJdhdzEeA8tVDbwsuR+OT\nb0wjenfQ6ic5GbM2EFXmnxpNfcv91zXsXgfNt8GtF00hHsLNEkIY1SQxSnpnuXUD\nBKuoo5QYfe97FqsA4/Jkzh+ztt0iWUbxIllu2t3T5jQs3I9ajrxcq5CUurGX2wR5\nZleEgd2utNHRnRMKibzNxRpJ+wALE7zVGgtiSUlzT49el4yF65MNr4hVODqYvmWh\n0dyDpSuntBTB/JqmQo0+\n=C9Yd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T18:41:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_ur