api.github.com/users/feanil/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feanil","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-authoring/commits/2cd75d19340e8a9bc03083260e40751dba5a4ade/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T19:16:11Z","email":"feanil@axim.org","name":"Feanil Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T20:35:51Z","email":"feanil@axim.org","name":"Feanil Patel"},"message":"feat!: remove marketingEnabled flag from Schedule & Details\n\nThe `marketingEnabled` field in the course settings API was previously driven\nby the `ENABLE_MKTG_SITE` backend setting, which has been removed in\nopenedx/openedx-platform#38720. The API now always returns `true`.\n\n- Remove `marketingEnabled` prop from `BasicSection`; always render the\n  promotional banner (the `true` path)\n- Extract the legacy enrollment card (LMS about-page link + \"Invite your\n  students\" mailto button) into a standalone `CoursePromotionCard` component\n  exported from `basic-section`, so operators can restore it via the\n  `PageBannerSlot` if desired\n- Extend `PageBannerSlot` to pass `lmsLinkForAboutPage`, `courseDisplayName`,\n  and `platformName` as `pluginProps` so `CoursePromotionCard` has what it needs\n  when used from a plugin\n- Update `PageBannerSlot` README with instructions for restoring the enrollment\n  card via the slot, and document the slot''s plugin props\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the \"Course summary page\" card is no longer shown by default\nwhen a marketing site is not configured. Operators can restore it via the\n`PageBannerSlot` using the exported `CoursePromotionCard` (see the slot README).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff61025824fb81c8705040ba5fd2f871066d1c7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-authoring/git/trees/ff61025824fb81c8705040ba5fd2f871066d1c7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/frontend-app-aut