odh-dashboard/commit/db444040f31c21bb153eb5a8f94fe9ebb0de1187","sha":"db444040f31c21bb153eb5a8f94fe9ebb0de1187","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/db444040f31c21bb153eb5a8f94fe9ebb0de1187"}],"sha":"c2b040d68ec369cfbe98310cc258af4dc205ecf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/c2b040d68ec369cfbe98310cc258af4dc205ecf7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12587674?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Gkrumbach07","id":12587674,"login":"Gkrumbach07","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTg3Njc0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gkrumbach07","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/db444040f31c21bb153eb5a8f94fe9ebb0de1187/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:28:40Z","email":"gkrumbac@redhat.com","name":"Gage Krumbach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:28:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(fullsend): brief reviewers with an investigator before dispatch (#10099)\n\n* feat(fullsend): brief reviewers with an investigator before dispatch\n\nReviewers each worked out what a change does from the raw diff, and\nnone was told which code outside the diff depends on it. A pre-dispatch\ncontext row now runs one investigator before the reviewer batch. Every\nlater LLM reviewer is told to read its brief, the challenger is not,\nand a missing brief never fails the review.\n\nAlso cap change_summary at 500 characters in the schema and trim it to\nthree sentences on the host.\n\nPorted from the fork trial, where three sandbox runs confirmed the step\nruns, the brief is written and read, and the challenger stays isolated.\n\nRHOAIENG-97762\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(fullsend): drop the host-side change summary trim\n\nThe result schema already rejects a change_summary over 500 characters,\nand the agent validates against it before the post-script runs. The\nthree-sentence trim in post-review.sh added 80 lines to enforce a limit\nthat 500 characters bounds anyway. post-review.sh is unchanged from main\nagain.\n\nRHOAIENG-97762\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(fullsend): keep the change summary cap to the schema''s maxLength\n\nDrop the description that repeated a sentence count. The schema''s\n500-character maxLength is the only limit this change adds.\n\nRHOAIENG-97762\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fcd0e7940a1691943421931ebc62f49245fdfea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/git/trees/4fcd0e7940a1691943421931ebc62f49245fdfea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/git/commits/db444040f31c21bb153eb5a8f94fe9ebb0de1187","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fcd0e7940a1691943421931ebc62f49245fdfea\nparent cd5a77916083f20866c5294e817e7e66c46c4fea\nauthor Gage Krumbach <gkrumbac@redhat.com> 1791307720 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791307720 +0000\n\nfeat(fullsend): brief reviewers with an investigator before dispatch (#10099)\n\n* feat(fullsend): brief reviewers with an investigator before dispatch\n\nReviewers each worked out what a change does from the raw diff, and\nnone was told which code outside the diff depends on it. A pre-dispatch\ncontext row now runs one investigator before the reviewer batch. Every\nlater LLM reviewer is told to read its brief, the challenger is not,\nand a missing brief never fails the review.\n\nAlso cap change_summary at 500 characters in the schema and trim it to\nthree sentences on the host.\n\nPorted from the fork trial, where three sandbox runs confirmed the step\nruns, the brief is written and read, and the challenger stays isolated.\n\nRHOAIENG-97762\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(fullsend): drop the host-side change summary trim\n\nThe result schema already rejects a change_summary over 500 characters,\nand the agent validates against it before the post-script runs. The\nthree-sentence trim in post-review.sh added 80 lines to enforce a limit\nthat 500 characters bounds anyway. post-review.sh is unchanged from main\nagain.\n\nRHOAIENG-97762\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(fullsend): keep the change summary cap to the schema''s maxLength\n\nDrop the description that repeated a sentence count. The schema''s\n500-character maxLength is the only limit this change adds.\n\nRHOAIENG-97762\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxS/ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4tIQAKEpM+jEH1D+8BHG9mVaq/NH\ny1FMewgsK7wJU0wgDCK0YtNCfh+a6r062Hbz3abTx2rLaxXbKQNWIi8AeO2hk+eS\nVX5Lv9/REeNtn1njCNXIJAm6xYzpQsKKeDYfrx++g6ZDxpaV5I9We+52WO7KBxET\nbvT6qxvOea8kCUXco3s7tiKd3Uut1mW+TBjsF2NWV26PjZEghn3AN/h3tuaJVrGg\nL/yMeiBjBc+utubxpDScR3/yZ/JVVAcozMiDlqDygA/mAa5O4OO7oUB13mtTa+UI\njCLD2mjkPpXF6RZ4y4QjZ7KRhWtuVdkiMsxrVlUiP+tQ/Qk/DhOzoR6JgDUmJp3a\nVPCd5dcCne/I7WaC1V0xfRflBqPV2TLkuWRQCAK7L06eqJ