:"6565b3007f572294bbf35d3017acdb2441813651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/6565b3007f572294bbf35d3017acdb2441813651"}],"sha":"8abea27cb0615ac54ecb1a7737ec4860d64cc66c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/8abea27cb0615ac54ecb1a7737ec4860d64cc66c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33689325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antowaddle","id":33689325,"login":"antowaddle","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjg5MzI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antowaddle","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/6565b3007f572294bbf35d3017acdb2441813651/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:26:21Z","email":"33689325+antowaddle@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anthony Coughlin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:26:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): support proxied ITUP Cypress runners (#10043)\n\n* ci: target ITUP Cypress runners\n\n* fix: add HTTPS proxy support to BFF proxyCall for egress-restricted runners\n\nproxyCall() uses Node''s native https.request() which does not respect\nHTTPS_PROXY env vars, causing all authenticated API calls to hang on\nself-hosted runners behind an egress proxy (Squid). Add https-proxy-agent\nto route requests through the proxy when HTTPS_PROXY is set, with\nNO_PROXY support.\n\nAlso set APP_ENV=development in the cypress:server:e2e script so DEV_MODE\nis enabled and the BFF reads the correct namespace from OC_PROJECT instead\nof parsing the kubeconfig context name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: pre-install Go BFF tooling and set MAAS_API_URL before E2E tests\n\nThe Go BFF servers download setup-envtest and K8s API binaries on first\nstart. When all BFFs start concurrently via Turbo, the parallel downloads\nrace and may not complete before the wait-on health checks time out,\ncausing the entire server process to exit and kill the test run.\n\nPre-install setup-envtest and download K8s 1.29.3 binaries in a\ndedicated step before the E2E tests run. Copy the binary into each BFF''s\nlocal bin directory so `make run` skips the download entirely.\n\nAlso derive MAAS_API_URL from the cluster ingress domain so the maas BFF\nskips its `oc get ingresses` auto-detection during startup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: expose BFF server output and add smoke test for startup debugging\n\nRemove --hide 0 from concurrently to expose server startup errors that\nwere previously invisible. Add smoke-test step that tests BFF prerequisites\n(go fmt, go vet, envtest, uv) individually before the main E2E run.\nAlso pre-download Go toolchain and warm module cache to prevent\nconcurrent downloads through the Squid proxy during startup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: fix EADDRINUSE by killing stale processes before E2E run\n\nRoot cause: the E2E proxy on port 4040 was left running from a\nprevious workflow run on this self-hosted runner. When the new run\ntried to bind to 4040, it got EADDRINUSE, which crashed process [0]\nin concurrently, triggering SIGTERM for all BFF servers.\n\nFix: add a cleanup step that kills any leftover processes on the\nE2E proxy port (4040) and all BFF ports (9100-9113) before starting.\nAlso removes the smoke-test step (diagnostic purpose served) and\nkills orphaned envtest processes (kube-apiserver, etcd).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: fix checkout failure when .git is missing on self-hosted runner\n\nThe checkout action''s \"Removing auth\" step fails with exit code 128\nwhen .git was deleted by a previous run. Re-init the repo in the\ncleanup step so checkout can clean up auth and proceed normally.\nAlso fix the chmod glob to include distributions/*/bff/bin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: add inline port cleanup right before server start to fix EADDRINUSE\n\nMove port cleanup from a separate step to inline in the Run E2E Tests\nstep, right before npx concurrently. This eliminates the 8-second gap\nbetween port cleanup and server start, during which a stale or zombie\nprocess could re-bind to port 4040.\n\nUses fuser -k for more reliable port release than lsof + kill.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): support proxied Cypress runners\n\n* fix(ci): harden proxy handling\n\n* fix(ci): hide backend request logs\n\n* fix(gen-ai): create Go temp dir for E2E\n\n* fix(backend): proxy Kubernetes websocket watches\n\n* test(e2e): quote PostgreSQL model-registry cleanup tables\n\n* test(e2e): route MaaS BFF via Squid-aware Cypress proxy\n\n* Use runner proxy for model registry E2E BFF requests\n\n* test(e2e): limit dashboard backend proxy to E2E runs\n\n* test(e2e): make MaaS proxy egress an opt-in\n\n(cherry picked from commit c5389bf3d06b27c921077bc9726c9814e9d70ee3)\n\n* fix(e2e): keep MaaS TLS untouched and type proxy options\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4eda27daff3d7bbb8838ed596cc3392e6115e5d3)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Fede Alonso <fealonso@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"80e58eb839bedbea4566707fd7ca8aceb0df0580","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/git/trees/80e58eb839bedbea4566707fd7ca8aceb0df0580"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/git/commits/6565b3007f572294bbf35d3017acdb2441813651","verification":{"payload":"tree 80e58eb839bedbea4566707fd7ca8aceb0df0580\nparent fa1bcdbf5d61a7efd4b83f3c36e9d61f591326b3\nauthor Anthony Coughlin <33689325+antowaddle@users.noreply.github.com> 1791282381 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791282381 +0000\n\ntest(e2e): support proxied ITUP Cypress runners (#10043)\n\n* ci: target ITUP Cypress runners\n\n* fix: add HTTPS proxy support to BFF proxyCall for egress-restricted runners\n\nproxyCall() uses Node''s native https.request() which does not respect\nHTTPS_PROXY env vars, causing all authenticated API calls to hang on\nself-hosted runners behind an egress proxy (Squid). Add https-proxy-agent\nto route requests through the proxy when HTTPS_PROXY is set, with\nNO_PROXY support.\n\nAlso set APP_ENV=development in the cypress:server:e2e script so DEV_MODE\nis enabled and the BFF reads the correct namespace from OC_PROJECT instead\nof parsing the kubeconfig context name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: pre-install Go BFF tooling and set MAAS_API_URL before E2E tests\n\nThe Go BFF servers download setup-envtest and K8s API binaries on first\nstart. When all BFFs start concurrently via Turbo, the parallel downloads\nrace and may not complete before the wait-on health checks time out,\ncausing the entire server process to exit and kill the test run.\n\nPre-install setup-envtest and download K8s 1.29.3 binaries in a\ndedicated step before the E2E tests run. Copy the binary into each BFF''s\nlocal bin directory so `make run` skips the download entirely.\n\nAlso derive MAAS_API_URL from the cluster ingress domain so the maas BFF\nskips its `oc get ingresses` auto-detection during startup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: expose BFF server output and add smoke test for startup debugging\n\nRemove --hide 0 from concurrently to expose server startup errors that\nwere previously invisible. Add smoke-test step that tests BFF prerequisites\n(go fmt, go vet, envtest, uv) individually before the main E2E run.\nAlso pre-download Go toolchain and warm module cache to prevent\nconcurrent downloads through the Squid proxy during startup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: fix EADDRINUSE by killing stale processes before E2E run\n\nRoot cause: the E2E proxy on port 4040 was left running from a\nprevious workflow run on this self-hosted runner. When the new run\ntried to bind to 4040, it got EADDRINUSE, which crashed process [0]\nin concurrently, triggering SIGTERM for all BFF servers.\n\nFix: add a cleanup step that kills any leftover processes on the\nE2E proxy port (4040) and all BFF ports (9100-9113) before starting.\nAlso removes the smoke-test step (diagnostic purpose served) and\nkills orphaned envtest processes (kube-apiserver, etcd).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: fix checkout failure when .git is missing on self-hosted runner\n\nThe checkout action''s \"Removing auth\" step fails with exit code 128\nwhen .git was deleted by a previous run. Re-init the repo in the\ncleanup step so checkout can clean up auth and proceed normally.\nAlso fix the chmod glob to include distributions/*/bff/bin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: add inline port cleanup right before server start to fix EADDRINUSE\n\nMove port cleanup from a separate step to inline in the Run E2E Tests\nstep, right before npx concurrently. This eliminates the 8-second gap\nbetween port cleanup and server start, during which a stale or zombie\nprocess could re-bind to port 4040.\n\nUses fuser -k for more reliable port release than lsof + kill.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): support proxied Cypress runners\n\n* fix(ci): harden proxy handling\n\n* fix(ci): hide backend request logs\n\n* fix(gen-ai): create Go temp dir for E2E\n\n* fix(backend): proxy Kubernetes websocket watches\n\n* test(e2e): quote PostgreSQL model-registry cleanup tables\n\n* test(e2e): route MaaS BFF via Squid-aware Cypress proxy\n\n* Use runner proxy for model registry E2E BFF requests\n\n* test(e2e): limit dashboard backend proxy to E2E runs\n\n* test(e2e): make MaaS proxy egress an opt-in\n\n(cherry picked from commit c5389bf3d06b27c921077bc9726c9814e9d70ee3)\n\n* fix(e2e): keep MaaS TLS untouched and type proxy options\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4eda27daff3d7bbb8838ed596cc3392e6115e5d3)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Fede Alonso <fealonso@redhat.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxMzNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAukYQAEgChso/GWR8dyDdyU1INK5T\n001a8yXd873HOVUS2DXSoE02KoPwRndb6+czqEroTEsiQOZmdehn4xFDAK3cFI/y\nRwK+1BnoUz0+jIOair7Q0Txpunnqolfe2/V9iSfZwo8OKEZAbtib1xocU/3Ae4Pe\nq3i7ZpdvQZpB7GBDCjRs57JMNcv2UkSw/gIfan5n7KeuUh2fhp3eYxB9H0Mv96QD\nZda9lRTZaZjrcT8DZNGqYoREwJ2BHe/p1KXVl4gUI4euGasHrTQZxxD7jlx+7IVE\n7j5F2Bs1X1ovTE5Z8TVzk//laiA2GCTEpSMpXWShqT/3w+EBQzk/+TwVelCcUb2k\n4G23gwSy/FLqlyHJE5K9AOYVVn6qoyIQIU5UkzjA0iJwlDj0ORG9/s+nRr6IJqFw\nrtca4Kb+dzqsE354G7Vdkd3qq8n4Qavw+5dR80LORuUOEvfj4sjuPnV1ifWjlOFM\nvssb0ZMS5fVoC88hgMbDyxfZYxfcPhVsVPV18LVQvhsx6CAfjSws0FOK22U0kyp5\nr8/K+R5RrKbpS876Naxz2BS7yPyXq+LjnNpG/3KBqtffbbip1CF9MVM2CRBO3EVw\nX/5arHmUecY2p2VcVxcp6/7nrip3Sr1yK7+QNAMXtda/G/QZhBr03fOVERHlt7bE\noNWcrn9OkKgK23PVJhgk\n=uZKR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T10:26:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","fol