ents","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commit/8212df60d0edc9d2a73634ed522fea048b5b46e1","node_id":"C_kwDOEAWiEdoAKDgyMTJkZjYwZDBlZGM5ZDJhNzM2MzRlZDUyMmZlYTA0OGI1YjQ2ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commit/ed5ee2e7fe69f8159c3673f87e600faeedd898ea","sha":"ed5ee2e7fe69f8159c3673f87e600faeedd898ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/ed5ee2e7fe69f8159c3673f87e600faeedd898ea"}],"sha":"8212df60d0edc9d2a73634ed522fea048b5b46e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/8212df60d0edc9d2a73634ed522fea048b5b46e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59457434?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daniduong","id":59457434,"login":"daniduong","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NDU3NDM0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniduong","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/commits/ed5ee2e7fe69f8159c3673f87e600faeedd898ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:19:47Z","email":"59457434+daniduong@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Daniel Duong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:19:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(autox-core): extract and deduplicate autox uis into autox-core (#9563)\n\n* feat(autox-core): fold ui into the autox-core workspace package and scaffold layered architecture\n\n- Add an exports map to packages/autox-core/package.json pointing at raw\n  ui/src/**/*.ts(x), mirroring the ui-core/k8s-core/plugin-core convention\n  (no build step, no dist/). This makes @odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/*\n  importable by automl and autorag via the existing workspace symlink and\n  Module Federation singleton auto-discovery.\n- Remove packages/autox-core/ui/package.json and package-lock.json: this\n  subfolder was previously structured as an isolated, unscoped npm project\n  (name ''autox-core-ui'', own node_modules) and was never actually\n  consumable as a workspace dependency. Scripts/deps are consolidated into\n  the top-level, already-correctly-wired autox-core package.json.\n- Simplify ui/tsconfig.json to extend the shared @odh-dashboard/tsconfig.\n- Add a babel-jest transform to ui/jest.config.js (previously had no\n  transform configured at all, so it silently never ran on real .ts files).\n- Scaffold ui/src/{api,hooks,layouts,components/{primitive,feature},utils}\n  with barrel index.ts files documenting each layer''s contract.\n- Add ui/ARCHITECTURE.md documenting the primitive -> feature (autox-core)\n  -> feature (product) -> layout -> page layering conventions, the\n  api/hooks domain-mirroring rule, cross-feature state escalation order,\n  and the autox-core-first scope boundary.\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract byte-identical topology primitives to autox-core/ui\n\nMove the topology helpers that were confirmed byte-identical (diffed\ndirectly, not just structurally similar) between automl and autorag into\nthe shared package:\n\n- topology/const.ts -> ui/src/utils/topology/const.ts\n- topology/tree-view/treeEdgePath.ts -> ui/src/utils/topology/treeEdgePath.ts\n- topology/tree-view/treeCaptionHeight.ts -> ui/src/hooks/topology/useBoundedCaptionHeight.ts\n  (renamed to match its primary hook export per naming convention)\n\nRewired the four remaining consumers in each package (topology/utils.ts,\ntree-view/TreeEdge.tsx, tree-view/TreeNode.tsx, and their tests) to import\nfrom @odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/{utils,hooks} instead of the local\nduplicate, then deleted the now-dead originals.\n\nDeliberately deferred: the rest of tree-view (branchExpand.ts,\ntransformPipelineData.ts, transformStageMapNodesToTree.ts, treeStepState.ts,\ntypes.ts, useTreeViewData.ts, TreeNode.scss, pulseAnimation.scss) bakes\nAutoML ''model'' vs AutoRAG ''pattern'' vocabulary directly into field/function\nnames and, for the two .scss files, uses genuinely different animation\nimplementations (not just renamed classes) — extracting those requires a\nreal generic-entity design pass plus visual QA, tracked separately rather\nthan rushed here.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean for both automl and autorag frontends; full\ntopology jest suites pass in both packages (278/278); new autox-core/ui\njest suite passes (6/6).\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract empty-states primitives to autox-core/ui\n\nMove the remaining self-contained (non-feature-layer) empty-state components\nfrom automl/autorag''s near-identical components/empty-states/ folders into\nautox-core/ui, parameterizing the AutoML/AutoRAG text differences via props\ninstead of hardcoding them:\n\n- PipelineServerStarting: byte-identical, moved verbatim.\n- InvalidExperiment, InvalidPipelineRun: add a productName prop.\n- NoProjects: add productName + icon props (icon stays product-owned since\n  it''s asset-backed and primitives must be fully props-controlled).\n- EnableManagedPipelinesModal: add a productName prop; still only consumed by\n  PipelineServerSetup, which stays local to each product (feature-layer,\n  needs the shared api/hooks layer for pipelines first) but now imports this\n  primitive from the shared package.\n- EmptyExperimentsState: replace the hardcoded title/description/iconImage\n  with props — AutoML and AutoRAG actually differ here (different icon\n  variant, different description copy), not just product name text.\n- AutomlRunInProgress/AutoragRunInProgress: merged into a single generic\n  RunInProgress primitive (productName + icon + viewRunsRoute props).\n\nAlso fixes a latent dual-module-instance bug this extraction exposed:\nautoml/autorag each have their own nested react-router/react-router-dom\ninstall (pinned to 7.18.1) that differs from the root install (7.18.2) that\n@odh-dashboard/autox-core (no node_modules of its own) always resolves\nagainst. A <MemoryRouter> from one copy and a <Link>/useNavigate from the\nother share no React context. Fixed the same way the existing react/react-dom\ndual-instance guard already does, in both packages'' jest.config.js.\n\nRewired every consumer (experiments pages, results/reconfigure pages,\nleaderboards) to import from ''@odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/components/primitive''\nand pass the new required props, updating jest.mock() calls that targeted the\nold local module paths to target the shared module path instead (using\njest.requireActual to preserve sibling exports from the same barrel).\n\nInvalidExperiment has no current consumer in either package (pre-existing\ndead code, now de-duplicated rather than fixed) — left as-is per the\nmigration inventory, not in scope to wire up or remove here.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean for automl, autorag, and autox-core/ui; full\nautoml (1623) and autorag (1767) jest suites pass; new autox-core/ui jest\nsuite passes (30/30, including new tests for previously-untested primitives).\n\n* refactor(autox-core): reclassify empty-state components as feature, extract real primitives\n\nThe previous batch (PipelineServerStarting, InvalidExperiment,\nInvalidPipelineRun, NoProjects, RunInProgress, EnableManagedPipelinesModal,\nEmptyExperimentsState) was misclassified as components/primitive/. Every one\nof them carried AutoX business vocabulary (Experiment, PipelineRun, managed\npipelines, Project) baked into hardcoded text or prop names, and two of them\n(PipelineServerStarting, EnableManagedPipelinesModal) directly imported\ndomain-specific internal modules (pipelinesBaseRoute,\nManagedPipelinesSettingsSection). None of that is portable to PatternFly, so\nnone of it qualifies as a primitive.\n\nMoved all 7 to components/feature/ and extracted the generic UI shells they\nwere built on top of as genuine, vocabulary-free primitives:\n\n- ActionableEmptyState: icon + title + body + optional single action button.\n  Backs InvalidExperiment, InvalidPipelineRun, NoProjects, RunInProgress.\n- SpinnerEmptyState: centered spinner + title + description + footer slot.\n  Backs PipelineServerStarting.\n- ConfirmationModal: modal shell with title, body slot, submit/cancel footer.\n  Backs EnableManagedPipelinesModal.\n\nThe 7 feature components are now thin wrappers supplying domain text/behavior\nto these primitives; EmptyExperimentsState needed no further extraction since\nit was already a thin wrapper around ui-core''s EmptyDetailsView.\n\nLoosens the ''feature'' layer definition to make hooks optional rather than a\ndefining trait: a feature is now anything AutoX-vocabulary-aware and reused\nacross AutoML/AutoRAG, whether or not it owns data via hooks (several of these\nuse useNavigate but that''s routing, not data-fetching). ARCHITECTURE.md and\nthe autox-core-ui-restructure-plan memory updated accordingly.\n\nNo behavior change for consumers — same rendered output, same props for the\n7 relocated components (just a different import path: components/feature\ninstead of components/primitive). Updated all automl/autorag consumer imports\nand jest.mock() targets accordingly.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean for automl, autorag, and autox-core/ui; full\nautoml (1623) and autorag (1767) jest suites pass; autox-core/ui jest suite\nnow at 45/45 (12 suites), including new tests for the 3 extracted primitives.\n\n* docs(autox-core): sharpen Primitive vs Feature (autox-core) definitions\n\nFollowing up on e280df4cc: a primitive must have zero business logic,\nconcepts, or terminology, not merely zero hooks. Documents the PatternFly-\nportability litmus test, explicit must-not/may lists, and reworks the Feature\n(autox-core) section so hooks are optional rather than a defining trait \\u2014\nwhat makes a component a feature is the AutoX vocabulary it carries, not\nwhether it owns a data-fetching hook. Updates all example lists and the\nimport snippet to reference the actually-verified primitives/features\n(ActionableEmptyState, SpinnerEmptyState, ConfirmationModal /\nInvalidExperiment, InvalidPipelineRun, NoProjects, RunInProgress,\nPipelineServerStarting, EnableManagedPipelinesModal, EmptyExperimentsState)\ninstead of not-yet-vetted forward-looking names.\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract ConfigureFormGroup, ContextBreadcrumb, ModuleHeader primitives\n\nExtracts three more genuinely vocabulary-free primitives from\npackages/automl/frontend and packages/autorag/frontend duplicates, per the\nsharpened Primitive litmus test from e280df4cc/fcd9b9a7b:\n\n- ConfigureFormGroup: generic labeled form-group wrapper with optional help\n  popover and description. Canonical = AutoRAG''s version (superset: adds\n  labelHelp.position, uses <Content component=\"small\"> for description).\n- ContextBreadcrumb (renamed from ExperimentContextBreadcrumb): breadcrumb for\n  pages nested under a project. Was byte-identical between automl/autorag\n  aside from a CSS class prefix; genericized the class name to\n  autox-breadcrumb-link-with-icon and replaced the internally-hardcoded\n  ''/projects/${namespace}'' route with a projectHomePath prop so the\n  component makes no assumption about app routing structure. Added\n  homeTestId/projectLinkTestId override props so existing consumer tests\n  keep passing unchanged against their prior testid strings.\n- ModuleHeader (new, replacing AutomlHeader/AutoragHeader internals): generic\n  icon-badge + label header. AutomlHeader/AutoragHeader are now two-line\n  product wrappers supplying their own icon and label text.\n\nSecretSelector and ProjectSelectorNavigator were evaluated for this batch and\ndeferred: both own data-fetching hooks (getSecrets/useNamespaceSelectorWithPersistence)\nand are entangled with the not-yet-migrated shared api/hooks layer (execution\nsequence stage 3), so pulling them in now risked a much larger, riskier change.\nTracked in the restructure-plan memory.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (automl, autorag, autox-core/ui); automl jest\n77 suites/1612 tests, autorag jest 84 suites/1756 tests, autox-core/ui jest\n15 suites/66 tests, all passing; eslint --max-warnings 0 clean on all touched\nfiles.\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract StopRunModal as a shared feature\n\nStopRunModal was byte-identical between automl/autorag aside from firing a\nper-product tracking event (AUTOML_EVENTS.RUN_STOPPED vs\nAUTORAG_EVENTS.RUN_STOPPED) when the modal is cancelled without an in-flight\nstop request. Extracted to components/feature/StopRunModal with the tracking\ncall replaced by an optional onCancel callback prop, so the shared component\ncarries no per-product tracking-catalog vocabulary. Kept the try/catch/finally\naround onConfirm (AutoML''s version, which AutoRAG''s had dropped, silently\nletting a rejected promise surface as an unhandled rejection) and the\nin-flight-submit cancel guard exactly as before.\n\nRewired all 4 consumer sites (AutomlResultsPage, AutomlRunsTableRow,\nAutoragResultsPage, AutoragRunsTableRow) to pass source-specific tracking via\nonCancel. Updated the two page-level jest mocks that stubbed\n''~/app/components/run-results/StopRunModal'' directly to instead add a\nStopRunModal export to the existing ''@odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/components/feature''\nmock block.\n\nAlso investigated ManageColumnsModal (a strong primitive candidate — fully\ngeneric column-management modal, AutoRAG''s version has a documented a11y fix)\nbut deferred it: it depends on @patternfly/react-component-groups and\n@patternfly/react-drag-drop, neither of which resolve for autox-core''s own\nlocal tsc/jest (only installed as nested deps inside automl/autorag''s own\nnode_modules). Adding them as new peerDependencies surfaces a large\nPRE-EXISTING, unrelated npm peer conflict already baked into the checked-in\nroot package-lock.json (observability package''s perses-dev peer graph vs\n@tanstack/react-query resolution) that requires --legacy-peer-deps and\nproduces a ~2400-line unrelated lockfile rewrite — too disruptive to fold in\nhere silently. Documented as a blocker in the restructure-plan memory,\npending explicit user sign-off on how to resolve it.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (automl, autorag, autox-core/ui); automl jest 76\nsuites/1599 tests, autorag jest 83 suites/1742 tests, autox-core/ui jest 16\nsuites/79 tests, all passing; eslint --max-warnings 0 clean on all touched\nfiles.\n\n* feat(autox-core): extract DeleteRunModal as a shared feature\n\nExtract DeleteRunModal to packages/autox-core/ui/src/components/feature,\ncanonicalizing on AutoRAG''s implementation per the AutoRAG-ahead rule: it\ncarried a race-condition fix (local isSubmitting state that flips\nsynchronously on Delete-click, before the async isDeleting prop updates)\nthat closes a gap where an immediate Escape/backdrop-close could otherwise\nslip past the busy guard. AutoML''s copy lacked this fix.\n\nDecouple the per-product tracking-catalog coupling the same way as\nStopRunModal: remove the internal fireFormTrackingEvent call and the\nsource: RunActionSource prop, replace with an optional onCancel callback\nsupplied by each consumer. Add a required productName prop for the modal\ntitle (\"Delete ${productName} optimization run?\"), following the pattern\nalready established by EnableManagedPipelinesModal/InvalidExperiment.\n\nThe previously-flagged source-prop divergence turned out to be a\nnon-issue: DeleteRunModal has exactly one consumer per product\n(Automl/AutoragRunsTableRow), and both always passed the literal\n''runsList''. RunActionSource itself stays in AutoRAG''s tracking.ts, still\nused elsewhere.\n\nRewire both AutomlRunsTableRow and AutoragRunsTableRow to import\nDeleteRunModal from @odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/components/feature\nalongside StopRunModal, and delete the duplicated product-local\ncomponents/specs. Port AutoRAG''s full race-condition test coverage into\nthe new shared spec.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (autox-core, automl, autorag); jest all\ngreen (autox-core 17/95, automl 75/1587, autorag 82/1727); eslint\n--max-warnings 0 clean on touched files.\n\n* feat(autox-core): promote AutoRAG''s UIError framework as a shared primitive\n\nPromote the entire UIError error-handling framework\n(types, UIErrorInstance, util helpers, UIErrorHandler context/provider,\nUIErrorAlert toast, UIErrorModal details dialog, and constants) from\npackages/autorag/frontend/src/app/components/common/UIError to\npackages/autox-core/ui/src/components/primitive/UIError.\n\nThe framework carries zero AutoRAG/AutoML business vocabulary — a fully\ngeneric error-envelope/toast/modal system any mod-arch BFF consumer could\nuse — matching the Primitive litmus test and ARCHITECTURE.md''s explicit\ncallout of this framework as a promotion candidate.\n\nNormalized the framework''s internal imports (dropped inconsistent\nexplicit .ts/.tsx extensions to match autox-core''s existing convention)\nbut made no other logic changes. Rewired all 9 AutoRAG consumers (App.tsx,\nodh/AppWrapper.tsx, AutoragConfigure.tsx, AutoragConfigurePage.tsx,\nautorag.uiErrorMappings.ts, api/s3.ts, hooks/mutations.ts, and 2 test\nharnesses) to import from @odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/components/primitive,\nmerging co-located imports from the same barrel where a file already\nimported another primitive from it. Deleted the old AutoRAG-local\ndirectory entirely, including its md doc (updated to reference the new\nimport path and note the still-local, not-yet-promoted Go-side\nNewUIError struct as a deferred follow-up).\n\nAdded mod-arch-core as an explicit dependency of @odh-dashboard/autox-core\n(version-matched to what automl/autorag already pin) and added it to the\njest transformIgnorePatterns allowlist, since UIError''s util.ts imports\nhandleRestFailures from it at module scope.\n\nAutoML does not yet integrate the UIError framework (no existing usage to\nmigrate) — wiring it up there is a product-level UX decision deferred to\nwhenever AutoML''s api layer adopts handleRestWithUIErrors.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (autox-core, autorag, automl unaffected);\njest all green (autox-core 20/158, autorag 79/1664, automl 75/1587);\neslint --max-warnings 0 clean on all touched files.\n\n* feat(autox-core): extract shared api/k8s, api/s3, api/pipelines\n\nPromote the near-duplicate k8s/S3/pipelines BFF API wrapper functions from\nautoml/autorag into packages/autox-core/ui/src/api/{k8s,s3,pipelines}/,\nalong with the shared types their signatures depend on.\n\nEach domain exposes a factory function (createK8sApi, createS3Api,\ncreatePipelinesApi) parameterized by a product''s BFF urlPrefix/API\nversion, since the endpoint paths are genuinely product-specific\n(/automl vs /autorag) but otherwise byte-identical. Each product''s local\napi/{k8s,s3,pipelines}.ts becomes a thin wrapper that instantiates the\nfactory with its own URL_PREFIX/BFF_API_VERSION constants and re-exports\nthe result — zero changes needed at any consumer of these api modules.\n\napi/k8s: getUser, getNamespaces, getSecrets extracted (getSecretByName,\ngetOgxModels, getOgxVectorStores stay local to AutoRAG — OGX-specific).\nWidened getSecrets'' secret-type param from AutoML''s ''storage'' / AutoRAG''s\n''storage'' | ''ogx'' literal unions to a plain optional string, since the\nset of valid secret types is a BFF/product concern the shared primitive\nshouldn''t encode.\n\napi/s3: uploadFileToS3, getFiles extracted. Deliberately migrated getFiles\nto handleRestWithUIErrors (AutoRAG had already migrated uploadFileToS3 but\nleft getFiles on the older handleRestFailures) — a genuine behavior\nimprovement applied to both products, not just a mechanical port.\nhandleRestWithUIErrors still falls back to handleRestFailures internally\nfor non-UIError-shaped failures, so this is a strict superset with no\nregression for either product.\n\napi/pipelines: getPipelineRunsFromBFF, getPipelineRunFromBFF,\nenableManagedPipelines extracted (getManagedPipelines,\ncreateIndexingPipelineRun, getPipelineDefinitions stay local to AutoRAG).\ncreatePipelinesApi is generic over TParams (a pipeline run''s\nruntime_config.parameters type) since AutoML''s BFF returns a\nstrongly-typed ConfigureSchema there while AutoRAG''s is an untyped bag —\nAutoML instantiates createPipelinesApi<ConfigureSchema>, AutoRAG uses the\nuntyped default. defaultPageSize is an optional factory param (default\n20) so AutoRAG no longer needs its own local DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE constant.\n\nShared types: added api/k8s/types.ts (NamespaceKind, SecretListItem),\napi/s3/types.ts (S3ObjectInfo, S3CommonPrefix, S3ListObjectsResponse),\nand api/pipelines/types.ts (PipelineVersionReference,\nPipelineRunRuntimeConfig<TParams>, PipelineRunError(Detail),\nPipelineRunTaskDetail, PipelineRunDetails, PipelineRunStateHistoryEntry,\nPipelineRun<TParams>, PipelineRunsData<TParams>,\nGetPipelineRunsFromBFFParams), all confirmed byte-identical between\nproducts apart from the TParams distinction. Each product''s types.ts now\naliases to these shared types instead of duplicating them.\n\nAlso extracted api/pipelines/kfTypes.ts, the KFP v2beta1 type subset\nduplicated verbatim in both products'' types/pipeline.ts (only their doc\ncomments differed). It''s intentionally NOT re-exported from the general\napi/index.ts barrel — it declares its own PipelineSpec (the full KFP\npipeline spec shape), which collides by name with api/pipelines/types.ts''s\nPipelineSpec (an alias for PipelineSpecVariable). Exposed instead via a\ndedicated package.json export subpath\n(@odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/api/pipelines/kfTypes). Each product''s\ntypes/pipeline.ts is now a thin re-export of it, so the many existing\ntopology/tree-view consumers of that import path are unaffected.\n\nDeleted automl/autorag''s api/__tests__/{s3,pipelines}.spec.ts — they only\nexercised logic now fully delegated to the shared factories, which have\ntheir own comprehensive test suites in autox-core (rewritten to construct\nthe factory directly with a test urlPrefix rather than jest.mock''ing each\nproduct''s utilities/const module). autorag''s api/__tests__/k8s.spec.ts is\nunchanged (it only covers the still-local getSecretByName).\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (autox-core, automl, autorag); jest all green\n(autox-core 23 suites/197 tests, automl 73/1575, autorag 77/1652); eslint\n--max-warnings 0 clean across all three packages.\n\n* feat(autox-core): extract shared hooks/common, hooks/k8s, hooks/pipelines\n\nPromote the near-duplicate generic hooks from automl/autorag into\npackages/autox-core/ui/src/hooks/{common,k8s,pipelines}/. Each product''s\nlocal hooks/*.ts file becomes a thin wrapper (import + re-export, or a\nfactory instantiation) — zero changes needed at any consumer of these\nhooks (same exported names, same import paths, same jest.mock() call\nsites keep working unchanged since they target the product-local path).\n\nhooks/common: useReconfigureSafeEffect, useNamespaceSelectorWithPersistence\nand usePreferredNamespaceRedirect were byte-identical (or differed only by\na doc-comment product name) and are shared verbatim as plain functions.\n\nuseUser and useNotification both depend on genuinely product-local state\n(each product''s own `AppContext` / notification zustand `store.ts`) that\nis deliberately NOT centralized here:\n- useUser is a `createUseUser(context)` factory parameterized by the\n  product''s own `React.Context` instance.\n- useNotification is a `createUseNotification(useAddNotification,\n  useRemoveNotification)` factory parameterized by the product''s own\n  store selectors. AutoML and AutoRAG are separate Module Federation\n  remotes that can both be mounted in the same host SPA session, and\n  `@odh-dashboard/autox-core` loads as a singleton shared dependency —\n  sharing one zustand store instance here would leak one product''s toast\n  notifications into the other''s `<ToastNotifications />` tree after an\n  in-SPA route change, so each product''s `store.ts` (and its\n  `AppNotification`/`AppNotificationAction` types) stays fully local and\n  untouched; only the ~140-line hook body wrapping it is shared.\n\nhooks/k8s/useNamespaces mirrors api/k8s the same way: a\n`createUseNamespaces(getNamespaces)` factory bound to the product''s own\nk8s API. Both `useNamespaces` and `useUser` are currently unused in both\nproducts (confirmed via a full consumer search) — extracted anyway per\nthe migration plan/1:1 api-hooks mirroring convention, not removed.\n\nhooks/pipelines/usePipelineRuns mirrors api/pipelines: a\n`createUsePipelineRuns<TParams>(getPipelineRunsFromBFF, defaultPageSize,\npollInterval)` factory, generic over the same `TParams` pipeline-run\nparameters type as `createPipelinesApi`. AutoML instantiates it with its\nown `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE`/`POLL_INTERVAL` consts (still product-local, since\n`utilities/const.ts` itself isn''t shared — URL_PREFIX is genuinely\nper-product); AutoRAG now drops its own local `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE = 20`\nredefinition entirely and relies on the factory''s own default.\n\nPorted test coverage for the byte-identical hooks (useReconfigureSafeEffect,\nuseNotification) into the new shared location and deleted the redundant\nproduct-local copies. Added fresh coverage for useNamespaceSelectorWithPersistence,\nusePreferredNamespaceRedirect, useUser, useNamespaces and usePipelineRuns,\nnone of which had product-local tests before (usePipelineRuns did — ported\nand adapted to the factory pattern; the other four are new).\n\nAlso fixed a latent dual-module-instance bug this batch exposed: automl''s\nand autorag''s own nested `mod-arch-core` installs are a different (older)\nversion than the root install `@odh-dashboard/autox-core` always resolves\nagainst (it has no node_modules of its own) — a `useModularArchContext`\ncreated by one copy doesn''t match the `ModularArchContextProvider` from\nthe other, breaking `useNamespaceSelector` for any consumer that now goes\nthrough the shared `useNamespaceSelectorWithPersistence`. Fixed via the\nsame moduleNameMapper pattern already used for the pre-existing\nreact/react-dom and react-router dual-instance guards, added to both\npackages'' jest.config.js. Also added `react-router` (previously only\n`react-router-dom`) as a peerDependency of `@odh-dashboard/autox-core`,\nneeded by the extracted `usePreferredNamespaceRedirect`.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (autox-core, automl, autorag); jest all green\n(autox-core 30 suites/243 tests, automl 70 suites/1540 tests, autorag 74\nsuites/1619 tests — one AutoragResults timeout flake under full-suite load,\nreproduced as passing in isolation and on re-run); eslint --max-warnings 0\n+ prettier clean across all three packages.\n\n* feat(autox-core): extract shared S3 and pipeline-run hooks\n\n* feat(autox-core): share product context across modules\n\n* refactor(autox-core): split pipeline and S3 hooks\n\n* refactor(autox-core): split aggregate hooks into per-file hooks\n\n* refactor(autox-core): use select for pipeline run normalization\n\n* refactor(autox-core): remove terminal state from product context\n\n* refactor(autox-core): remove error status from product context\n\n* refactor(autox-core): inject API clients via context\n\n* refactor(autox-core): own API client construction in provider\n\n* refactor(autox-core): simplify default pipeline page size\n\n* refactor(autox-core): share pipeline run creation hook\n\n* refactor(autox-core): cache reusable S3 reads\n\n* refactor(autox-core): await React Query invalidation\n\n* refactor(autox-core): remove lodash dependencies\n\n* refactor(autox-core): update package dependencies\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract ManageColumnsModal primitive\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract project navigation features\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract shared secret selector\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract shared connection modal\n\n* fix(autox-core): clean up api/hooks boundaries\n\n* fix(autox-core): internalize api boundaries\n\n* chore: update package.json\n\n* fix(autox-core): preflight issues\n\n* test: fix path used in usePipelineRuns.spec.ts\n\n* chore: fix build errors, update Dockerfile.workspace\n\n* fix(autox-core): address review\n\n* fix: address review\n\n* fix(autox-core): address comments\n\n* test: fix test regressions and flakes","tree":{"sha":"3f9a4a8d46cf46977828e86457bc3b6c733b45c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/git/trees/3f9a4a8d46cf46977828e86457bc3b6c733b45c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard/git/commits/ed5ee2e7fe69f8159c3673f87e600faeedd898ea","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f9a4a8d46cf46977828e86457bc3b6c733b45c8\nparent 3af08ed56148e4289945197a94214ec6171041de\nauthor Daniel Duong <59457434+daniduong@users.noreply.github.com> 1790803187 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790803187 +0000\n\nfeat(autox-core): extract and deduplicate autox uis into autox-core (#9563)\n\n* feat(autox-core): fold ui into the autox-core workspace package and scaffold layered architecture\n\n- Add an exports map to packages/autox-core/package.json pointing at raw\n  ui/src/**/*.ts(x), mirroring the ui-core/k8s-core/plugin-core convention\n  (no build step, no dist/). This makes @odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/*\n  importable by automl and autorag via the existing workspace symlink and\n  Module Federation singleton auto-discovery.\n- Remove packages/autox-core/ui/package.json and package-lock.json: this\n  subfolder was previously structured as an isolated, unscoped npm project\n  (name ''autox-core-ui'', own node_modules) and was never actually\n  consumable as a workspace dependency. Scripts/deps are consolidated into\n  the top-level, already-correctly-wired autox-core package.json.\n- Simplify ui/tsconfig.json to extend the shared @odh-dashboard/tsconfig.\n- Add a babel-jest transform to ui/jest.config.js (previously had no\n  transform configured at all, so it silently never ran on real .ts files).\n- Scaffold ui/src/{api,hooks,layouts,components/{primitive,feature},utils}\n  with barrel index.ts files documenting each layer''s contract.\n- Add ui/ARCHITECTURE.md documenting the primitive -> feature (autox-core)\n  -> feature (product) -> layout -> page layering conventions, the\n  api/hooks domain-mirroring rule, cross-feature state escalation order,\n  and the autox-core-first scope boundary.\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract byte-identical topology primitives to autox-core/ui\n\nMove the topology helpers that were confirmed byte-identical (diffed\ndirectly, not just structurally similar) between automl and autorag into\nthe shared package:\n\n- topology/const.ts -> ui/src/utils/topology/const.ts\n- topology/tree-view/treeEdgePath.ts -> ui/src/utils/topology/treeEdgePath.ts\n- topology/tree-view/treeCaptionHeight.ts -> ui/src/hooks/topology/useBoundedCaptionHeight.ts\n  (renamed to match its primary hook export per naming convention)\n\nRewired the four remaining consumers in each package (topology/utils.ts,\ntree-view/TreeEdge.tsx, tree-view/TreeNode.tsx, and their tests) to import\nfrom @odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/{utils,hooks} instead of the local\nduplicate, then deleted the now-dead originals.\n\nDeliberately deferred: the rest of tree-view (branchExpand.ts,\ntransformPipelineData.ts, transformStageMapNodesToTree.ts, treeStepState.ts,\ntypes.ts, useTreeViewData.ts, TreeNode.scss, pulseAnimation.scss) bakes\nAutoML ''model'' vs AutoRAG ''pattern'' vocabulary directly into field/function\nnames and, for the two .scss files, uses genuinely different animation\nimplementations (not just renamed classes) — extracting those requires a\nreal generic-entity design pass plus visual QA, tracked separately rather\nthan rushed here.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean for both automl and autorag frontends; full\ntopology jest suites pass in both packages (278/278); new autox-core/ui\njest suite passes (6/6).\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract empty-states primitives to autox-core/ui\n\nMove the remaining self-contained (non-feature-layer) empty-state components\nfrom automl/autorag''s near-identical components/empty-states/ folders into\nautox-core/ui, parameterizing the AutoML/AutoRAG text differences via props\ninstead of hardcoding them:\n\n- PipelineServerStarting: byte-identical, moved verbatim.\n- InvalidExperiment, InvalidPipelineRun: add a productName prop.\n- NoProjects: add productName + icon props (icon stays product-owned since\n  it''s asset-backed and primitives must be fully props-controlled).\n- EnableManagedPipelinesModal: add a productName prop; still only consumed by\n  PipelineServerSetup, which stays local to each product (feature-layer,\n  needs the shared api/hooks layer for pipelines first) but now imports this\n  primitive from the shared package.\n- EmptyExperimentsState: replace the hardcoded title/description/iconImage\n  with props — AutoML and AutoRAG actually differ here (different icon\n  variant, different description copy), not just product name text.\n- AutomlRunInProgress/AutoragRunInProgress: merged into a single generic\n  RunInProgress primitive (productName + icon + viewRunsRoute props).\n\nAlso fixes a latent dual-module-instance bug this extraction exposed:\nautoml/autorag each have their own nested react-router/react-router-dom\ninstall (pinned to 7.18.1) that differs from the root install (7.18.2) that\n@odh-dashboard/autox-core (no node_modules of its own) always resolves\nagainst. A <MemoryRouter> from one copy and a <Link>/useNavigate from the\nother share no React context. Fixed the same way the existing react/react-dom\ndual-instance guard already does, in both packages'' jest.config.js.\n\nRewired every consumer (experiments pages, results/reconfigure pages,\nleaderboards) to import from ''@odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/components/primitive''\nand pass the new required props, updating jest.mock() calls that targeted the\nold local module paths to target the shared module path instead (using\njest.requireActual to preserve sibling exports from the same barrel).\n\nInvalidExperiment has no current consumer in either package (pre-existing\ndead code, now de-duplicated rather than fixed) — left as-is per the\nmigration inventory, not in scope to wire up or remove here.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean for automl, autorag, and autox-core/ui; full\nautoml (1623) and autorag (1767) jest suites pass; new autox-core/ui jest\nsuite passes (30/30, including new tests for previously-untested primitives).\n\n* refactor(autox-core): reclassify empty-state components as feature, extract real primitives\n\nThe previous batch (PipelineServerStarting, InvalidExperiment,\nInvalidPipelineRun, NoProjects, RunInProgress, EnableManagedPipelinesModal,\nEmptyExperimentsState) was misclassified as components/primitive/. Every one\nof them carried AutoX business vocabulary (Experiment, PipelineRun, managed\npipelines, Project) baked into hardcoded text or prop names, and two of them\n(PipelineServerStarting, EnableManagedPipelinesModal) directly imported\ndomain-specific internal modules (pipelinesBaseRoute,\nManagedPipelinesSettingsSection). None of that is portable to PatternFly, so\nnone of it qualifies as a primitive.\n\nMoved all 7 to components/feature/ and extracted the generic UI shells they\nwere built on top of as genuine, vocabulary-free primitives:\n\n- ActionableEmptyState: icon + title + body + optional single action button.\n  Backs InvalidExperiment, InvalidPipelineRun, NoProjects, RunInProgress.\n- SpinnerEmptyState: centered spinner + title + description + footer slot.\n  Backs PipelineServerStarting.\n- ConfirmationModal: modal shell with title, body slot, submit/cancel footer.\n  Backs EnableManagedPipelinesModal.\n\nThe 7 feature components are now thin wrappers supplying domain text/behavior\nto these primitives; EmptyExperimentsState needed no further extraction since\nit was already a thin wrapper around ui-core''s EmptyDetailsView.\n\nLoosens the ''feature'' layer definition to make hooks optional rather than a\ndefining trait: a feature is now anything AutoX-vocabulary-aware and reused\nacross AutoML/AutoRAG, whether or not it owns data via hooks (several of these\nuse useNavigate but that''s routing, not data-fetching). ARCHITECTURE.md and\nthe autox-core-ui-restructure-plan memory updated accordingly.\n\nNo behavior change for consumers — same rendered output, same props for the\n7 relocated components (just a different import path: components/feature\ninstead of components/primitive). Updated all automl/autorag consumer imports\nand jest.mock() targets accordingly.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean for automl, autorag, and autox-core/ui; full\nautoml (1623) and autorag (1767) jest suites pass; autox-core/ui jest suite\nnow at 45/45 (12 suites), including new tests for the 3 extracted primitives.\n\n* docs(autox-core): sharpen Primitive vs Feature (autox-core) definitions\n\nFollowing up on e280df4cc: a primitive must have zero business logic,\nconcepts, or terminology, not merely zero hooks. Documents the PatternFly-\nportability litmus test, explicit must-not/may lists, and reworks the Feature\n(autox-core) section so hooks are optional rather than a defining trait \\u2014\nwhat makes a component a feature is the AutoX vocabulary it carries, not\nwhether it owns a data-fetching hook. Updates all example lists and the\nimport snippet to reference the actually-verified primitives/features\n(ActionableEmptyState, SpinnerEmptyState, ConfirmationModal /\nInvalidExperiment, InvalidPipelineRun, NoProjects, RunInProgress,\nPipelineServerStarting, EnableManagedPipelinesModal, EmptyExperimentsState)\ninstead of not-yet-vetted forward-looking names.\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract ConfigureFormGroup, ContextBreadcrumb, ModuleHeader primitives\n\nExtracts three more genuinely vocabulary-free primitives from\npackages/automl/frontend and packages/autorag/frontend duplicates, per the\nsharpened Primitive litmus test from e280df4cc/fcd9b9a7b:\n\n- ConfigureFormGroup: generic labeled form-group wrapper with optional help\n  popover and description. Canonical = AutoRAG''s version (superset: adds\n  labelHelp.position, uses <Content component=\"small\"> for description).\n- ContextBreadcrumb (renamed from ExperimentContextBreadcrumb): breadcrumb for\n  pages nested under a project. Was byte-identical between automl/autorag\n  aside from a CSS class prefix; genericized the class name to\n  autox-breadcrumb-link-with-icon and replaced the internally-hardcoded\n  ''/projects/${namespace}'' route with a projectHomePath prop so the\n  component makes no assumption about app routing structure. Added\n  homeTestId/projectLinkTestId override props so existing consumer tests\n  keep passing unchanged against their prior testid strings.\n- ModuleHeader (new, replacing AutomlHeader/AutoragHeader internals): generic\n  icon-badge + label header. AutomlHeader/AutoragHeader are now two-line\n  product wrappers supplying their own icon and label text.\n\nSecretSelector and ProjectSelectorNavigator were evaluated for this batch and\ndeferred: both own data-fetching hooks (getSecrets/useNamespaceSelectorWithPersistence)\nand are entangled with the not-yet-migrated shared api/hooks layer (execution\nsequence stage 3), so pulling them in now risked a much larger, riskier change.\nTracked in the restructure-plan memory.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (automl, autorag, autox-core/ui); automl jest\n77 suites/1612 tests, autorag jest 84 suites/1756 tests, autox-core/ui jest\n15 suites/66 tests, all passing; eslint --max-warnings 0 clean on all touched\nfiles.\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract StopRunModal as a shared feature\n\nStopRunModal was byte-identical between automl/autorag aside from firing a\nper-product tracking event (AUTOML_EVENTS.RUN_STOPPED vs\nAUTORAG_EVENTS.RUN_STOPPED) when the modal is cancelled without an in-flight\nstop request. Extracted to components/feature/StopRunModal with the tracking\ncall replaced by an optional onCancel callback prop, so the shared component\ncarries no per-product tracking-catalog vocabulary. Kept the try/catch/finally\naround onConfirm (AutoML''s version, which AutoRAG''s had dropped, silently\nletting a rejected promise surface as an unhandled rejection) and the\nin-flight-submit cancel guard exactly as before.\n\nRewired all 4 consumer sites (AutomlResultsPage, AutomlRunsTableRow,\nAutoragResultsPage, AutoragRunsTableRow) to pass source-specific tracking via\nonCancel. Updated the two page-level jest mocks that stubbed\n''~/app/components/run-results/StopRunModal'' directly to instead add a\nStopRunModal export to the existing ''@odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/components/feature''\nmock block.\n\nAlso investigated ManageColumnsModal (a strong primitive candidate — fully\ngeneric column-management modal, AutoRAG''s version has a documented a11y fix)\nbut deferred it: it depends on @patternfly/react-component-groups and\n@patternfly/react-drag-drop, neither of which resolve for autox-core''s own\nlocal tsc/jest (only installed as nested deps inside automl/autorag''s own\nnode_modules). Adding them as new peerDependencies surfaces a large\nPRE-EXISTING, unrelated npm peer conflict already baked into the checked-in\nroot package-lock.json (observability package''s perses-dev peer graph vs\n@tanstack/react-query resolution) that requires --legacy-peer-deps and\nproduces a ~2400-line unrelated lockfile rewrite — too disruptive to fold in\nhere silently. Documented as a blocker in the restructure-plan memory,\npending explicit user sign-off on how to resolve it.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (automl, autorag, autox-core/ui); automl jest 76\nsuites/1599 tests, autorag jest 83 suites/1742 tests, autox-core/ui jest 16\nsuites/79 tests, all passing; eslint --max-warnings 0 clean on all touched\nfiles.\n\n* feat(autox-core): extract DeleteRunModal as a shared feature\n\nExtract DeleteRunModal to packages/autox-core/ui/src/components/feature,\ncanonicalizing on AutoRAG''s implementation per the AutoRAG-ahead rule: it\ncarried a race-condition fix (local isSubmitting state that flips\nsynchronously on Delete-click, before the async isDeleting prop updates)\nthat closes a gap where an immediate Escape/backdrop-close could otherwise\nslip past the busy guard. AutoML''s copy lacked this fix.\n\nDecouple the per-product tracking-catalog coupling the same way as\nStopRunModal: remove the internal fireFormTrackingEvent call and the\nsource: RunActionSource prop, replace with an optional onCancel callback\nsupplied by each consumer. Add a required productName prop for the modal\ntitle (\"Delete ${productName} optimization run?\"), following the pattern\nalready established by EnableManagedPipelinesModal/InvalidExperiment.\n\nThe previously-flagged source-prop divergence turned out to be a\nnon-issue: DeleteRunModal has exactly one consumer per product\n(Automl/AutoragRunsTableRow), and both always passed the literal\n''runsList''. RunActionSource itself stays in AutoRAG''s tracking.ts, still\nused elsewhere.\n\nRewire both AutomlRunsTableRow and AutoragRunsTableRow to import\nDeleteRunModal from @odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/components/feature\nalongside StopRunModal, and delete the duplicated product-local\ncomponents/specs. Port AutoRAG''s full race-condition test coverage into\nthe new shared spec.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (autox-core, automl, autorag); jest all\ngreen (autox-core 17/95, automl 75/1587, autorag 82/1727); eslint\n--max-warnings 0 clean on touched files.\n\n* feat(autox-core): promote AutoRAG''s UIError framework as a shared primitive\n\nPromote the entire UIError error-handling framework\n(types, UIErrorInstance, util helpers, UIErrorHandler context/provider,\nUIErrorAlert toast, UIErrorModal details dialog, and constants) from\npackages/autorag/frontend/src/app/components/common/UIError to\npackages/autox-core/ui/src/components/primitive/UIError.\n\nThe framework carries zero AutoRAG/AutoML business vocabulary — a fully\ngeneric error-envelope/toast/modal system any mod-arch BFF consumer could\nuse — matching the Primitive litmus test and ARCHITECTURE.md''s explicit\ncallout of this framework as a promotion candidate.\n\nNormalized the framework''s internal imports (dropped inconsistent\nexplicit .ts/.tsx extensions to match autox-core''s existing convention)\nbut made no other logic changes. Rewired all 9 AutoRAG consumers (App.tsx,\nodh/AppWrapper.tsx, AutoragConfigure.tsx, AutoragConfigurePage.tsx,\nautorag.uiErrorMappings.ts, api/s3.ts, hooks/mutations.ts, and 2 test\nharnesses) to import from @odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/components/primitive,\nmerging co-located imports from the same barrel where a file already\nimported another primitive from it. Deleted the old AutoRAG-local\ndirectory entirely, including its md doc (updated to reference the new\nimport path and note the still-local, not-yet-promoted Go-side\nNewUIError struct as a deferred follow-up).\n\nAdded mod-arch-core as an explicit dependency of @odh-dashboard/autox-core\n(version-matched to what automl/autorag already pin) and added it to the\njest transformIgnorePatterns allowlist, since UIError''s util.ts imports\nhandleRestFailures from it at module scope.\n\nAutoML does not yet integrate the UIError framework (no existing usage to\nmigrate) — wiring it up there is a product-level UX decision deferred to\nwhenever AutoML''s api layer adopts handleRestWithUIErrors.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (autox-core, autorag, automl unaffected);\njest all green (autox-core 20/158, autorag 79/1664, automl 75/1587);\neslint --max-warnings 0 clean on all touched files.\n\n* feat(autox-core): extract shared api/k8s, api/s3, api/pipelines\n\nPromote the near-duplicate k8s/S3/pipelines BFF API wrapper functions from\nautoml/autorag into packages/autox-core/ui/src/api/{k8s,s3,pipelines}/,\nalong with the shared types their signatures depend on.\n\nEach domain exposes a factory function (createK8sApi, createS3Api,\ncreatePipelinesApi) parameterized by a product''s BFF urlPrefix/API\nversion, since the endpoint paths are genuinely product-specific\n(/automl vs /autorag) but otherwise byte-identical. Each product''s local\napi/{k8s,s3,pipelines}.ts becomes a thin wrapper that instantiates the\nfactory with its own URL_PREFIX/BFF_API_VERSION constants and re-exports\nthe result — zero changes needed at any consumer of these api modules.\n\napi/k8s: getUser, getNamespaces, getSecrets extracted (getSecretByName,\ngetOgxModels, getOgxVectorStores stay local to AutoRAG — OGX-specific).\nWidened getSecrets'' secret-type param from AutoML''s ''storage'' / AutoRAG''s\n''storage'' | ''ogx'' literal unions to a plain optional string, since the\nset of valid secret types is a BFF/product concern the shared primitive\nshouldn''t encode.\n\napi/s3: uploadFileToS3, getFiles extracted. Deliberately migrated getFiles\nto handleRestWithUIErrors (AutoRAG had already migrated uploadFileToS3 but\nleft getFiles on the older handleRestFailures) — a genuine behavior\nimprovement applied to both products, not just a mechanical port.\nhandleRestWithUIErrors still falls back to handleRestFailures internally\nfor non-UIError-shaped failures, so this is a strict superset with no\nregression for either product.\n\napi/pipelines: getPipelineRunsFromBFF, getPipelineRunFromBFF,\nenableManagedPipelines extracted (getManagedPipelines,\ncreateIndexingPipelineRun, getPipelineDefinitions stay local to AutoRAG).\ncreatePipelinesApi is generic over TParams (a pipeline run''s\nruntime_config.parameters type) since AutoML''s BFF returns a\nstrongly-typed ConfigureSchema there while AutoRAG''s is an untyped bag —\nAutoML instantiates createPipelinesApi<ConfigureSchema>, AutoRAG uses the\nuntyped default. defaultPageSize is an optional factory param (default\n20) so AutoRAG no longer needs its own local DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE constant.\n\nShared types: added api/k8s/types.ts (NamespaceKind, SecretListItem),\napi/s3/types.ts (S3ObjectInfo, S3CommonPrefix, S3ListObjectsResponse),\nand api/pipelines/types.ts (PipelineVersionReference,\nPipelineRunRuntimeConfig<TParams>, PipelineRunError(Detail),\nPipelineRunTaskDetail, PipelineRunDetails, PipelineRunStateHistoryEntry,\nPipelineRun<TParams>, PipelineRunsData<TParams>,\nGetPipelineRunsFromBFFParams), all confirmed byte-identical between\nproducts apart from the TParams distinction. Each product''s types.ts now\naliases to these shared types instead of duplicating them.\n\nAlso extracted api/pipelines/kfTypes.ts, the KFP v2beta1 type subset\nduplicated verbatim in both products'' types/pipeline.ts (only their doc\ncomments differed). It''s intentionally NOT re-exported from the general\napi/index.ts barrel — it declares its own PipelineSpec (the full KFP\npipeline spec shape), which collides by name with api/pipelines/types.ts''s\nPipelineSpec (an alias for PipelineSpecVariable). Exposed instead via a\ndedicated package.json export subpath\n(@odh-dashboard/autox-core/ui/api/pipelines/kfTypes). Each product''s\ntypes/pipeline.ts is now a thin re-export of it, so the many existing\ntopology/tree-view consumers of that import path are unaffected.\n\nDeleted automl/autorag''s api/__tests__/{s3,pipelines}.spec.ts — they only\nexercised logic now fully delegated to the shared factories, which have\ntheir own comprehensive test suites in autox-core (rewritten to construct\nthe factory directly with a test urlPrefix rather than jest.mock''ing each\nproduct''s utilities/const module). autorag''s api/__tests__/k8s.spec.ts is\nunchanged (it only covers the still-local getSecretByName).\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (autox-core, automl, autorag); jest all green\n(autox-core 23 suites/197 tests, automl 73/1575, autorag 77/1652); eslint\n--max-warnings 0 clean across all three packages.\n\n* feat(autox-core): extract shared hooks/common, hooks/k8s, hooks/pipelines\n\nPromote the near-duplicate generic hooks from automl/autorag into\npackages/autox-core/ui/src/hooks/{common,k8s,pipelines}/. Each product''s\nlocal hooks/*.ts file becomes a thin wrapper (import + re-export, or a\nfactory instantiation) — zero changes needed at any consumer of these\nhooks (same exported names, same import paths, same jest.mock() call\nsites keep working unchanged since they target the product-local path).\n\nhooks/common: useReconfigureSafeEffect, useNamespaceSelectorWithPersistence\nand usePreferredNamespaceRedirect were byte-identical (or differed only by\na doc-comment product name) and are shared verbatim as plain functions.\n\nuseUser and useNotification both depend on genuinely product-local state\n(each product''s own `AppContext` / notification zustand `store.ts`) that\nis deliberately NOT centralized here:\n- useUser is a `createUseUser(context)` factory parameterized by the\n  product''s own `React.Context` instance.\n- useNotification is a `createUseNotification(useAddNotification,\n  useRemoveNotification)` factory parameterized by the product''s own\n  store selectors. AutoML and AutoRAG are separate Module Federation\n  remotes that can both be mounted in the same host SPA session, and\n  `@odh-dashboard/autox-core` loads as a singleton shared dependency —\n  sharing one zustand store instance here would leak one product''s toast\n  notifications into the other''s `<ToastNotifications />` tree after an\n  in-SPA route change, so each product''s `store.ts` (and its\n  `AppNotification`/`AppNotificationAction` types) stays fully local and\n  untouched; only the ~140-line hook body wrapping it is shared.\n\nhooks/k8s/useNamespaces mirrors api/k8s the same way: a\n`createUseNamespaces(getNamespaces)` factory bound to the product''s own\nk8s API. Both `useNamespaces` and `useUser` are currently unused in both\nproducts (confirmed via a full consumer search) — extracted anyway per\nthe migration plan/1:1 api-hooks mirroring convention, not removed.\n\nhooks/pipelines/usePipelineRuns mirrors api/pipelines: a\n`createUsePipelineRuns<TParams>(getPipelineRunsFromBFF, defaultPageSize,\npollInterval)` factory, generic over the same `TParams` pipeline-run\nparameters type as `createPipelinesApi`. AutoML instantiates it with its\nown `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE`/`POLL_INTERVAL` consts (still product-local, since\n`utilities/const.ts` itself isn''t shared — URL_PREFIX is genuinely\nper-product); AutoRAG now drops its own local `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE = 20`\nredefinition entirely and relies on the factory''s own default.\n\nPorted test coverage for the byte-identical hooks (useReconfigureSafeEffect,\nuseNotification) into the new shared location and deleted the redundant\nproduct-local copies. Added fresh coverage for useNamespaceSelectorWithPersistence,\nusePreferredNamespaceRedirect, useUser, useNamespaces and usePipelineRuns,\nnone of which had product-local tests before (usePipelineRuns did — ported\nand adapted to the factory pattern; the other four are new).\n\nAlso fixed a latent dual-module-instance bug this batch exposed: automl''s\nand autorag''s own nested `mod-arch-core` installs are a different (older)\nversion than the root install `@odh-dashboard/autox-core` always resolves\nagainst (it has no node_modules of its own) — a `useModularArchContext`\ncreated by one copy doesn''t match the `ModularArchContextProvider` from\nthe other, breaking `useNamespaceSelector` for any consumer that now goes\nthrough the shared `useNamespaceSelectorWithPersistence`. Fixed via the\nsame moduleNameMapper pattern already used for the pre-existing\nreact/react-dom and react-router dual-instance guards, added to both\npackages'' jest.config.js. Also added `react-router` (previously only\n`react-router-dom`) as a peerDependency of `@odh-dashboard/autox-core`,\nneeded by the extracted `usePreferredNamespaceRedirect`.\n\nVerified: tsc --noEmit clean (autox-core, automl, autorag); jest all green\n(autox-core 30 suites/243 tests, automl 70 suites/1540 tests, autorag 74\nsuites/1619 tests — one AutoragResults timeout flake under full-suite load,\nreproduced as passing in isolation and on re-run); eslint --max-warnings 0\n+ prettier clean across all three packages.\n\n* feat(autox-core): extract shared S3 and pipeline-run hooks\n\n* feat(autox-core): share product context across modules\n\n* refactor(autox-core): split pipeline and S3 hooks\n\n* refactor(autox-core): split aggregate hooks into per-file hooks\n\n* refactor(autox-core): use select for pipeline run normalization\n\n* refactor(autox-core): remove terminal state from product context\n\n* refactor(autox-core): remove error status from product context\n\n* refactor(autox-core): inject API clients via context\n\n* refactor(autox-core): own API client construction in provider\n\n* refactor(autox-core): simplify default pipeline page size\n\n* refactor(autox-core): share pipeline run creation hook\n\n* refactor(autox-core): cache reusable S3 reads\n\n* refactor(autox-core): await React Query invalidation\n\n* refactor(autox-core): remove lodash dependencies\n\n* refactor(autox-core): update package dependencies\n\n* refactor(autox-core): extract Manag